<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Guatavita</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Guatavita is a small circular lake in the eastern Andes of Colombia, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a>, sacred to the Muisca. In the installation of a new ruler, the chief was covered in gold dust and made offerings of gold on a raft in the lake, the origin of the legend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-dorado">El Dorado</a>. Spanish and later treasure hunters tried repeatedly to drain it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-guatavita.jpg" alt="Lake Guatavita" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Masanalv · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LagunaDeGuatavita.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
